{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For tsav le-tsav.</b> They are worthy that one speak with them as a father speaks to his small son, who does not yet know." "<b>Tsav le-tsav.</b> Commandment after commandment, or a commandment joined to a commandment." "<b>Kav le-kav.</b> Learning of writing." "<b>Ze'ir sham.</b> A little, a little, time after time."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:34.538264191Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}